    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW217gn4wLNpoCYemQ7ducAoe)_\n\nBefore: there was no record of what changed in the Emacs config apart from the PR list and git history.\n\nAfter: `.config/emacs-modular/CHANGELOG.org` has one entry for each of PRs #1 to #10. Entries are grouped by merge date (newest first) and then by Added, Changed or Fixed. Each entry names the modules it touched and links its PR. There is also an \"Open pull requests\" section, which is empty for now.\n\nHow: each entry is written from the PR's \"After:\" paragraph and its list of changed files. When a PR touched a whole directory, the entry says so rather than listing every file (#2, #6, #10). The one long list, the 14 docs renamed to `-old.org` in #2, is a sub-list under its entry, so `TAB` folds it. The file is written to the format of the `dotfiles-changelog` skill.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01XXsSZQBCESX1iv9iD21FVu)_",
